  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid S1P receptor modulators: Mayzent (siponimod), Ponvory (ponesimod), Zeposia (ozanimod), Velsipity (etrasimod). Version 3; approval 01/19/2024; effective 2024-03-01.",
    "Encoded: MS and UC approval criteria 1-7 and all denial criteria. Failure to meet approval is handled by approval predicates. Closed product-gated indications; clinical workup, history and adequate prior trial/failure are attestations.",
    "Cautions (notes only): infection risk; macular edema risk with uveitis or diabetes mellitus; Posterior Reversible Encephalopathy Syndrome (PRES); basal cell carcinoma and other skin malignancies; bradyarrhythmia and atrioventricular conduction delays; avoid live attenuated vaccines for up to 4 weeks after treatment; concomitant moderate CYP2C9 and moderate to strong CYP3A4 inhibitors and inducers not recommended.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 6 months; reauthorization approval up to 12 months.",
    "Quantity (notes only): 34-day supply. No numeric quantity enforcement.",
    "PDL status unknown. MS peer alternatives require separate eligibility evaluation and are not UC alternatives. The separate Mayzent pack retains its own source criteria.",
    "Remaining gaps: documentation verification, cautions, duration, reauthorization, dosing and quantity enforcement require manual review."
  ],
